Stochastic monotonicity in Young graph and Thoma
theorem.
Alexey Bufetov∗
Vadim Gorin†
November 13, 2014
Abstract
We show that the order on probability measures, inherited from the dominance
order on the Young diagrams, is preserved under natural maps reducing the number
of boxes in a diagram by 1. As a corollary we give a new proof of the Thoma theorem
on the structure of characters of the inﬁnite symmetric group.
We present several conjectures generalizing our result.
One of them (if it is
true) would imply the Kerov’s conjecture on the classiﬁcation of all homomorphisms
from the algebra of symmetric functions into R which are non-negative on Hall–
Littlewood polynomials.
